# Frontend Development Patterns

## React & TypeScript
- Functional components with TypeScript interfaces
- Use React.FC for type annotations, prefer composition
- Keep components single-purpose

## State Management
- Use Zustand stores for global state
- Custom hooks for reusable state logic
- Use selectors to prevent unnecessary re-renders

## Material-UI & Styling
- Use Material-UI components consistently
- Use sx prop for component-specific styling
- Mobile-first design with Material-UI breakpoints

## API Integration & Services
- Use Axios for HTTP requests with error handling
- TypeScript interfaces for responses
- Place services in [services/](mdc:frontend/src/services/)
- Global error handling with interceptors

## Custom Hooks & Utilities
- Create custom hooks for reusable logic
- Place in [hooks/](mdc:frontend/src/hooks/) and [utils/](mdc:frontend/src/utils/)
- Use TypeScript for type safety

## Form Handling & File Upload
- Use controlled components with validation
- Material-UI form components
- Drag-and-drop file upload with validation
- Show upload progress and clear error messages

## Performance & Optimization
- React.memo for expensive components
- useMemo and useCallback for calculations
- Dynamic imports for code splitting
- Lazy loading for routes

## Testing
- React Testing Library for components
- Test user interactions and accessibility
- Mock external dependencies

## Code Organization
- Group related components, use index files
- Import organization: React, third-party, local, types
- TypeScript strict mode, avoid `any` type
